meta {
  name: Apple Invalid Token (401)
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/apple
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "identityToken": "not.a.jwt",
    "nonce": "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"
  }
}

docs {
  Expect 401 {"error": "Invalid Apple identity token"}.

  The same 401 covers every rejection — bad signature, wrong issuer, an
  audience that is not our bundle id, an expired token, a token older than 10
  minutes, and a nonce that does not match. Distinguishing them would tell an
  attacker which check to work on next.

  Worth trying by hand: mint a token signed with your own key carrying
  iss=https://appleid.apple.com and aud=samgro.Hackysack. It must still be
  rejected, because the signature is checked against Apple's published JWKS.
}
